# Table

A styled data table. Compose it from `Table`, `TableHeader`, `TableBody`, `TableFooter`, `TableRow`, `TableHead`, `TableCell`, and `TableCaption`, which render the matching native table elements.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Table, TableHeader, TableBody, TableFooter, TableRow, TableHead, TableCell, TableCaption } from "#lib/components/ui/table/index.js";

	const invoices = [
		{ id: "INV001", status: "Paid", method: "Credit Card", amount: "$250.00" },
		{ id: "INV002", status: "Pending", method: "PayPal", amount: "$150.00" },
	];
</script>

<Table>
	<TableCaption>A list of your recent invoices.</TableCaption>
	<TableHeader>
		<TableRow>
			<TableHead>Invoice</TableHead>
			<TableHead>Status</TableHead>
			<TableHead>Method</TableHead>
			<TableHead style="text-align: right">Amount</TableHead>
		</TableRow>
	</TableHeader>
	<TableBody>
		{#each invoices as invoice (invoice.id)}
			<TableRow>
				<TableCell>{invoice.id}</TableCell>
				<TableCell>{invoice.status}</TableCell>
				<TableCell>{invoice.method}</TableCell>
				<TableCell style="text-align: right">{invoice.amount}</TableCell>
			</TableRow>
		{/each}
	</TableBody>
	<TableFooter>
		<TableRow>
			<TableCell colspan={3}>Total</TableCell>
			<TableCell style="text-align: right">$400.00</TableCell>
		</TableRow>
	</TableFooter>
</Table>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/table.json
```

## Anatomy

`Table` renders a `div` that scrolls sideways when the table is wider than its container, with the `table` inside it. The `class` and other attributes go on the `table`. Header rows keep a bottom border, body rows are divided by borders, and the footer sits on a muted background. `TableCaption` renders a `caption` under the rows, which screen readers announce as the table's title.

Cells do not wrap their text. Set `white-space` on a cell through `class` or `style` when a column holds long text.

## Row selection

Place a `Checkbox` in the first column, and set `data-state="selected"` on a `TableRow` to highlight it. Cells that hold a checkbox drop their end padding so the column stays narrow.

<Demo section="selection" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Table, TableHeader, TableBody, TableRow, TableHead, TableCell } from "#lib/components/ui/table/index.js";
	import { Checkbox } from "#lib/components/ui/checkbox/index.js";

	let selectedIds: string[] = $state([]);
</script>

<Table>
	<TableHeader>
		<TableRow>
			<TableHead>
				<Checkbox aria-label="Select all invoices" checked={selectedIds.length === invoices.length} onCheckedChange={(checked) => (selectedIds = checked ? invoices.map((invoice) => invoice.id) : [])} />
			</TableHead>
			<TableHead>Invoice</TableHead>
		</TableRow>
	</TableHeader>
	<TableBody>
		{#each invoices as invoice (invoice.id)}
			{@const isSelected = selectedIds.includes(invoice.id)}
			<TableRow data-state={isSelected ? "selected" : undefined}>
				<TableCell>
					<Checkbox aria-label="Select {invoice.id}" checked={isSelected} onCheckedChange={(checked) => (selectedIds = checked ? [...selectedIds, invoice.id] : selectedIds.filter((id) => id !== invoice.id))} />
				</TableCell>
				<TableCell>{invoice.id}</TableCell>
			</TableRow>
		{/each}
	</TableBody>
</Table>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` on `Table` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, with 40 pixel header rows and 8 pixel cell padding like the shadcn table. The header height, cell padding, and text size follow the size. The table has no box of its own, so there is no `rounded` prop.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Table size="sm">...</Table>
```

## API

`Table` extends the native `table` attributes, and every other part extends the attributes of the element it renders: `thead`, `tbody`, `tfoot`, `tr`, `th`, `td`, and `caption`.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"table"> {
	/** Row height, cell padding, and text size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
}

interface HeaderProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"thead"> {}

interface BodyProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"tbody"> {}

interface FooterProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"tfoot"> {}

interface RowProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"tr"> {}

interface HeadProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"th"> {}

interface CellProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"td"> {}

interface CaptionProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"caption"> {}
```
